~ start
Mentor: Today you learn what sets a tamer apart from everyone else.
Mentor: We track. We observe. We wait. Then — and only then — we act.
Kael: Are we hunting something?
Mentor: We're offering something a home.
=> END

~ den_found
Mentor: There. The den.
Mentor: The mother won't survive. But the young one can.
Mentor: This is the moment, Kael. Everything I've taught you — it lives in your hands right now.
=> END

~ taming_prompt
Mentor: Clear your mind. Feel the rhythm. Match it.
=> END

~ taming_success
Mentor: You did it.
Kael: It worked?
Mentor: It always works when you stop trying to make it work.
Mentor: Now — give it a name. That's yours from this moment on.
=> END

~ commands_lesson
Mentor: Listen carefully. There are five commands every tamer must know.
Mentor: Follow. Stay. Scout. Recall. Attack.
Mentor: Your companion understands more than words — they understand your intent. But the words anchor that intent. Practice them.
=> END

~ quest_complete
Mentor: You're a tamer now.
Mentor: If I tell you to run, you run. No questions.
=> END
